  title={From Static Platforms to Intelligent Assistants: Reviewing LMS Challenges and the Role of Retrieval Augmented Generation}, 
  year={2025},
  volume={},
  number={},
  pages={1-8},
  abstract={In higher education, Learning Management Systems (LMS) provide a tightly controlled central access to academic materials, assignment and communication services. They are however, deficient in that they can hardly assist students in real-time and in a personalised manner which causes delays in communications and more faculty workload. The formerly established methods of reinforcing the work of LMS are rule based chatbots and AI powered assistants, yet they can be either deprived of contextual information or provide mistaken answers without sound grounds. The review will discuss the shortcomings of the conventional LMS courseware and understand how the new emerging technologies, and specifically Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG) are facilitating a change in the digital learning landscape. This approach can be used in place of traditional AI tools to deliver more precise, contextualized answers through the merging of document retrieval with natural language generation, which is something RAG is able to accomplish. Our method aggregates the available literature on AI LMS combination, contrasts existing patterns, and analyses the plausibility of such a system in the classroom environment by means of RAG based systems. The paper features the major user experience enhancements, query processing, and administrative efficiencies, which can serve as a guide to the future development of AI based LMSs.},
  keywords={Learning management systems;Semantic search;Reviews;Query processing;Retrieval augmented generation;Natural language generation;Chatbots;Vectors;User experience;Real-time systems;Learning Management System (LMS);Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG);AI Chatbots in Education;Educational Technology;Personalized Learning Support;Semantic Search and Vector Database},
