  title={XOR-TOPK : Efficient Top-K Selection Hardware Engine Based on Bitwise XOR Operation}, 
  year={2026},
  volume={},
  number={},
  pages={1-1},
  abstract={Top-k selection is one of the most widely used algorithms, aiming to identify the largest or smallest k elements in an input sequence. Numerous applications demand dedicated hardware to accelerate top-k operations. While prior works focus on algorithmic complexity, hardware cost depends heavily on operation types. This work exploits the low-cost nature of bitwise XOR operations to design a high-efficiency top-k architecture, termed XOR-TOPK. The proposed design is modular and scalable, supporting various input sizes with low latency and area overhead. Compared with state-of-the-art designs, XOR-TOPK achieves up to 1.46×–19.7× reductions in area–delay and power–delay products for large-scale inputs. When integrated into a dynamic sparsity accelerator, it further reduces the area and latency of token selection stage, demonstrating strong potential for emerging applications.},
